<section id="faq" class="faq" style="border-top:1px solid var(--line)"><div class="w">
<h2 class="d">Questions &amp; answers</h2>
<div style="max-width:760px">
<details open><summary>Who can attend Yashasvi Bhav?</summary><p>Students of Class 10th and Class 12th. The programme is built around their board examinations.</p></details>
<details><summary>Is it really free?</summary><p>Yes. Yashasvi Bhav is completely free of cost.</p></details>
<details><summary>How do I register?</summary><p>Students can register themselves by filling in the <a href="https://forms.gle/gviixmhqx3rbcfty9" target="_blank" rel="noopener">registration form</a>. It takes only a few minutes.</p></details>
<details><summary>When are the events?</summary><p>Chikhali on 5 December 2026, Nigdi on 12 December 2026, Maval on 19 December 2026 and Chakan on 26 December 2026.</p></details>
<details><summary>How will I get venue and timing details?</summary><p>Join the Yashasvi Bhav WhatsApp group. Venue and timing details, event reminders and important announcements are shared there.</p></details>
<details><summary>What will I get from the programme?</summary><p>Important questions and a question bank, study guidance, answer writing techniques, doubt-solving sessions, guidance from experienced teachers and time management tips.</p></details>
<details><summary>Which subjects are covered?</summary><p>Class 10th: English, Marathi, Hindi, Mathematics, Science and Social Science. Class 12th: Science, Commerce and Arts. The guidance is subject-wise and exam-oriented.</p></details>
<details><summary>Who organises Yashasvi Bhav?</summary><p>Lions International and Steps Foundation, together with associate partners including schools, institutes and social foundations.</p></details>
<details><summary>Who do I contact if I need help?</summary><p>Call <a href="tel:+918446600051">84466 00051</a> or follow Steps Foundation on Instagram and Facebook for updates.</p></details>
</div>
</div></section>

